// The Interface "color book": every colorway of every style on the Keim dealer
// price list (8.19.25 edition), keyed by the style name exactly as the sheet
// prints it (cross-format twins under one base name; LVT thickness editions
// under their own printed names). Transcribed from shop.interface.com's US
// product pages on 2026-08-27 — the same registry the physical sample deck
// mirrors — because the price list itself carries no colors and the orderable
// unit is style + colorway (docs/pricebook/interface.md).
//
// Each entry: `no` is Interface's style number (the shop's product id — 9628C
// = Open Air 401), `colors` is [colorNumber, colorName, quickShip?] — the
// color number is the other half of the orderable identity ("9628C 107689" =
// Open Air 401, Amber), and a trailing 1 marks a colorway Interface lists in
// its QuickShip program. Two price-list styles (HN830, OVEREDGE) are not on
// the shop site and have no entry — they import style-only.
//
// Colorway ranges shift seasonally. To refresh: re-run the scrape
// (.scratch/114_interface-carpet-tile/colorbook-scrape.py) and replace this
// file wholesale; interfacebook.js joins it at import time, so the book picks
// the changes up on the next price-list re-import.
